{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For the sake of</b> — it is joined to <b>arise YHWH</b>." "<b>Do not turn away the face of Your anointed</b> — he is David, for the meaning is doubled like <b>משפט</b>. He explained the meaning of <b>for the sake of</b>, and this is <b>נשבע</b>. The meaning is as I have said, for the names are in the power of the verbs."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 132, :notes {1 "The referents of משפט and נשבע are unclear; possibly scribal abbreviations or corruptions. Transmitted hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:36.757423265Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}